  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="fdca-2908-b151-5ffe" name="Crusaders (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>CRUSADER ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.40-41): the major Crusading movements or the field armies of the Crusader states.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Cavalry up to three quarters of the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Special Troops &amp; Allies up to a quarter, with one artillery piece per 500 points.
Military Orders: if any Military Order troops are fielded, two units of Military Order mounted knights (Brethren) must be used (Military Order foot may only be taken with them; not enforced). On the battlefield, if one Military Order knight unit charges an enemy, the other automatically charges its nearest enemy (or, if none is within reach, moves at least 4" towards the nearest enemy).
Combined Formations: crossbowmen may be combined with other infantry (dismounted knights or spearmen of the same origin) in a single regiment, initially making up the front ranks. On entering close combat the crossbowmen either stay in front (standing and shooting at a charging enemy; spear-armed figures in the second rank may fight) or retire to the rear (no shooting, but up to two full ranks of spearmen or one rank of other infantry fight); bringing them forward again costs a turn reforming.
Allies (not built here: make a separate small roster): troops from the Byzantine and Arab &amp; Saracen lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: up to 75%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Special Troops &amp; Allies: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
